      {
        "id": "li0111_republican_001_m",
        "name": "Republican Shipping\n Andreas Heilmann",
        "idsName": "220097",
        "affiliation": "co_rs_grp",
        "voice": "rvp146",
        "rumors": [
          "Ich lege eine kurze Pause ein, bevor ich die letzte Etappe nach Pittsburgh fliege. Ich habe Bergbaumaschinen aus Essen geladen. Auf dem Rückweg nach Sugarland nehmen wir Bor mit.",
          "Ich habe Berlin schon vor Wochen verlassen; wir wurden sage und schreibe fünfmal überfallen. Ich werde langsam zu alt für sowas. Normalerweise transportieren wir Kobalt und Kupfer vom Ring zum großen Ageira-Werk in Colorado. Manchmal befördern wir auch Bergbaumaschinen aus Essen nach Pittsburgh.",
          "Die Xenos stellen im südlichen New York eigentlich kein Problem dar. Höchstens die Rogues, und manchmal Ausgestoßene. Wir Rheinländer bekommen es nicht oft mit ihnen zu tun. Korsaren und Rote Hessen -- ja, das ist was anderes. Ich habe meinem Chef schon gesagt, \"Nach Omega-7 fliege ich nicht mehr -- ich will mein Rentenalter noch erreichen.\"",
          "Have you heard the news about Schultzky? He was attacked right here in Liberty! No matter what the news tells you, I hear the LSF knows exactly who did it, but won't tell us. They probably also know who destroyed Freeport 7. I wonder what they’re trying to cover up.",
          "You know what I heard? The planetary defense grid around Manhattan was sabotaged. That’s how The Order managed to get through to Schultzky’s ship. It’s frightening what these people can pull off. They must have people helping them on the inside.",
          "I've never even heard of \"The Order\" before the whole Schultzky incident. I'm no expert but I find it difficult to believe that the LSF, who is supposed to be protecting our interests and who we already know has a deep intelligence channel, didn't know much about the attack. How could they not see this coming? Well at least they got the Rogues around Pittsburgh. That's something.",
          "The President apparently called Bonnerille and the LSF on the carpet for the whole Schultzky screw up. The Chancellor is furious, holding us responsible for Schultzky's death. There's a rumor floating around that Intelligence knew more about The Order than they are letting on.",
          "Well, the first analysis of the Freeport 7 data has just been made available. From what I have heard so far, the station’s defense systems didn’t fire one shot at the attacking ships. Either the radar system of the station didn’t pick up the attackers, or someone on the inside disabled the defense systems. Could be that there was a traitor on board."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "li0111_samura_001_m",
        "name": "Samura Heavy Industries\n Akio Hagawa",
        "idsName": "220098",
        "affiliation": "co_shi_grp",
        "voice": "rvp126",
        "rumors": [
          "Wir sind eine uralte Firma, die kurz nach der Gründung Kusaris entstand. Wir haben so lange überdauert, weil wir ausgezeichnete Produkte herstellen. Der H-Treibstoff aus Osaka, mit dem wir diese Basis versorgen, ist von höchster Qualität.",
          "Ich verlasse nur ungern das Kusari-Gebiet, um unsere Produkte hier in Liberty an die Gaijin zu verscherbeln, aber ich muss ja irgendwie wieder gutmachen, dass ich letztes Jahr bei der Sakura-Feier versehentlich eins der wertvollen Xeno-Artefakte unseres Generaldirektors zerbrochen habe.",
          "Liberty nimmt Samuras Transportprobleme offensichtlich nicht ernst. Unsere Frachter werden ständig von Xenos überfallen, aber die libertanische Regierung tut praktisch nichts dagegen. Wo ist denn ihre Marine? Die kümmert sich doch nur um den südlichen Sektor von New York, und uns soll die LPI beschützen.",
          "Have you heard the news about Schultzky? He was attacked right here in Liberty! No matter what the news tells you, I hear the LSF knows exactly who did it, but won't tell us. They probably also know who destroyed Freeport 7. I wonder what they’re trying to cover up.",
          "You know what I heard? The planetary defense grid around Manhattan was sabotaged. That’s how The Order managed to get through to Schultzky’s ship. It’s frightening what these people can pull off. They must have people helping them on the inside.",
          "I've never even heard of \"The Order\" before the whole Schultzky incident. I'm no expert but I find it difficult to believe that the LSF, who is supposed to be protecting our interests and who we already know has a deep intelligence channel, didn't know much about the attack. How could they not see this coming? Well at least they got the Rogues around Pittsburgh. That's something.",
          "The President apparently called Bonnerille and the LSF on the carpet for the whole Schultzky screw up. The Chancellor is furious, holding us responsible for Schultzky's death. There's a rumor floating around that Intelligence knew more about The Order than they are letting on.",
          "Well, the first analysis of the Freeport 7 data has just been made available. From what I have heard so far, the station’s defense systems didn’t fire one shot at the attacking ships. Either the radar system of the station didn’t pick up the attackers, or someone on the inside disabled the defense systems. Could be that there was a traitor on board."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "li0111_synth_001_m",
        "name": "Synth Foods\n Luke Stillwell",
        "idsName": "220099",
        "affiliation": "co_ni_grp",
        "voice": "rvp101",
        "rumors": [
          "Hey, was schmeckt besser als ein Fass voll Paste? Stimmt -- nichts in Sirius, das weniger als ein halbes Monatsgehalt kostet. Wer so richtigen Heißhunger auf Nahrungspaste hat, der wende sich getrost an mich.",
          "Dieser Punkt markiert die Hälfte meiner Strecke von Los Angeles nach Denver. Für die Stützpunkte in dieser Gegend von Liberty bringen wir meist ein bisschen was extra mit. Ich habe diese Synth-Paste ja so satt. Man bekommt das Zeug billiger, wenn man für den Hersteller arbeitet. Die Manager bekommen natürlich Luxuslebensmittel aus Stuttgart kostenlos an die Haustür geliefert. Ja, das nenn' ich Service.",
          "Unsere Biosphären wachsen überall in Sirius aus dem Boden; unsere Fachleute bauen die allerbesten Luxuslebensmittel in Stuttgart an.",
          "Have you heard the news about Schultzky? He was attacked right here in Liberty! No matter what the news tells you, I hear the LSF knows exactly who did it, but won't tell us. They probably also know who destroyed Freeport 7. I wonder what they’re trying to cover up.",
          "You know what I heard? The planetary defense grid around Manhattan was sabotaged. That’s how The Order managed to get through to Schultzky’s ship. It’s frightening what these people can pull off. They must have people helping them on the inside.",
          "I've never even heard of \"The Order\" before the whole Schultzky incident. I'm no expert but I find it difficult to believe that the LSF, who is supposed to be protecting our interests and who we already know has a deep intelligence channel, didn't know much about the attack. How could they not see this coming? Well at least they got the Rogues around Pittsburgh. That's something.",
          "The President apparently called Bonnerille and the LSF on the carpet for the whole Schultzky screw up. The Chancellor is furious, holding us responsible for Schultzky's death. There's a rumor floating around that Intelligence knew more about The Order than they are letting on.",
          "Well, the first analysis of the Freeport 7 data has just been made available. From what I have heard so far, the station’s defense systems didn’t fire one shot at the attacking ships. Either the radar system of the station didn’t pick up the attackers, or someone on the inside disabled the defense systems. Could be that there was a traitor on board."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "li0111_universal_001_m",
        "name": "Universal Shipping\n Jack Buckner",
        "idsName": "220100",
        "affiliation": "co_ss_grp",
        "voice": "rvp101",
        "rumors": [
          "Universal Shipping ist die wichtigste Spedition in Liberty. Wir bringen Grundlegierungen, Konsumgüter und Kobalt aus Texas, Wasser und Sauerstoff aus Manhattan und Bor aus Pittsburgh.",
          "Pittsburgh bezieht einen Großteil seiner Vorräte von dieser Basis. Universal bringt Sauerstoff, Lebensmittel, Wasser, Bergbaumaschinen, H-Treibstoff, Pharmazeutika und Verbrauchsgüter dorthin.",
          "Dies ist ein Umschlagplatz für Baumaschinen, die von Texas nach Colorado verfrachtet werden, und für Bor aus Pittsburgh, das nach Sugarland und Pueblo geht.",
          "Ft. Bush dient als New Yorks zweitgrößter Verteilerhafen für H-Treibstoff und Optronik aus Kusari. Von hier aus beliefern wir Houston und Militärstützpunkte im Südosten des Systems.",
          "Have you heard the news about Schultzky? He was attacked right here in Liberty! No matter what the news tells you, I hear the LSF knows exactly who did it, but won't tell us. They probably also know who destroyed Freeport 7. I wonder what they’re trying to cover up.",
          "You know what I heard? The planetary defense grid around Manhattan was sabotaged. That’s how The Order managed to get through to Schultzky’s ship. It’s frightening what these people can pull off. They must have people helping them on the inside.",
          "I've never even heard of \"The Order\" before the whole Schultzky incident. I'm no expert but I find it difficult to believe that the LSF, who is supposed to be protecting our interests and who we already know has a deep intelligence channel, didn't know much about the attack. How could they not see this coming? Well at least they got the Rogues around Pittsburgh. That's something.",
          "The President apparently called Bonnerille and the LSF on the carpet for the whole Schultzky screw up. The Chancellor is furious, holding us responsible for Schultzky's death. There's a rumor floating around that Intelligence knew more about The Order than they are letting on."
        ]
      }
